  dialogueText: 'Click! Great pose!

    It''s warm today, and you might want something
    refreshing.

    In Ilokano, ''uminom'' means ''drink.''

    It is an action
    verb used when talking about drinking something.

    Listen carefully: uminom.

    Now,
    try saying ''uminom'' yourself.'
